+## §16b THE CORPS — A FREE COMPANY CARRIES THE MARK (CH-10)
+
+[CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — `RULINGS-ROUND2.md` B and `briefs/L-CH.md`'s addendum: the owner's word of 2026-10-18 ~07:3x, verbatim, "Mercenaries are fine as is. And effectively can be emulated or used for our champion system just replace a champion with a corp", ruled by the chair as THE CORPS; a new section and OD-CH-36.]
+
+**What it is.** The paragon's mark may sit on a free COMPANY as well as on a person: `authored.holderKind: person · corps`. A corps is the WAR calling (`domain: war`) of either side, FREE (for hire) by default or BOUND to a court, and it lives exactly as a paragon does — the weekly choice ("until a better deal or reason comes along"), retainers both ways (§7), fame, regard and deeds (RN), bans and the town's gate (§11), the hearings (§18) — with three differences: it is a UNIT, not a person; it never holds custody; and its strength is a band its unit carries.
+
+**Its record — WC's free unit, never a new ledger.** The mark is ONE conditional, drop-when-empty `paragon` field on WC's free-unit record (`spatialLedgers.freeUnits[unitKey]`, `DESIGN_FP_ARCH_WC.md` §1.7.2: `{ blocks, position, state, supplyBand, driftBand, beliefStaleness }`, `FREE_UNIT_STATES` `operating · foraging · raiding · dissolving`), normalized by the same leaf `normalizeParagon` in WC's free-unit normalizer, landed in the commit of its first writer (CH2's law, for a second host). "No parallel NPC system" holds for both kinds: a corps is WC's unit, a person the ledger's. MOVEMENT AND BATTLE RIDE WC's UNIT UNION — the free unit's own army-style stepper and WC's battles; a captain paragon who rides with it mirrors its leg (the co-location read, CH8). Its weekly choice sets the unit's destination through WC's one stepper (one physics; the corps adds no speed).
+
+**Born only by the DM.** A corps is DM-authored (custom content; the `introduce` door with `holderKind: corps`), NEVER engine-born: WC's fission products stay unmarked free units, and the engine never promotes one (CH1). Its PEOPLE are never conjured: they come from the census of the origin settlement the DM names, through a WC-registered, DM-authority people-ledger event (one manpower truth; WC's conservation walker judges it) — a WC inbox row, since WC's free units are born only by fission today. Its strength band is WC's band of its blocks.
+
+**Hire without merger.** A corps hires out at the price of trust (its retainer's `termsBand`, §7) and NEVER joins the hirer's manpower pool: its blocks stay its own, so the hirer's census, levy and `mercSupplementOf` are untouched ("Mercenaries are fine as is"). Retained, it marches beside or ahead of the hirer's host; its GIFT is the war calling's lean at ITS OWN strength band — the §6.2 war row on the unit record (its own quality in WC's battle read) and, attached to the hirer's army, the captain's per-battle term on that army record — SLOT C4 (the generals design) with WC's free units.
+
+**Failure, death and custody.** A corps' failure ladder is `setback` (the lean does not apply) · `stumble` (fame dips) · `desertion` (its strength band falls one, the shed blocks taking WC's own dissolution road) · `sell-out` — the top rung: it breaks its retainer and turns on its employer, a `sold_out` deed (§2.2b's act table, villainous on its face, so the villain side's consequences follow — bans, the scandal of regard, no court's trust), heard as `paragon_disgraced` with the corps' sentence on the card (`disgraced` = the sale stands; `weathered` = the DM spares it). A lost battle is WC's (casualties lower its band). NO CUSTODY ROAD: a company is defeated or disbanded, never held. DEATH = DISBANDMENT, THE DM'S: the DM's own act ends it (CH's door, a `disband` arm beside `introduce` for `holderKind: corps`; the free unit enters WC's `dissolving` state and its people re-enter WC's shed road); the engine never disbands a marked company — a corps whittled to nothing stands on its page with no men until the DM decides.
 
+**Who it is to the world.** Its actor ref is `{ kind: 'corps', id: unitKey }`: a cross-volume row for the fold — SP-4a's `POSTURE_ACTOR_KINDS` gains `corps` (as it gained `site`), the exclusion edge's actor-ref widening (PT's shape change) gains a `corps` arm, and RN keys its fame and regard as `c:<unitKey>` beside `p:<wnpc>` (RN's registration). Its name ("the Grey Company") is the DM's, quoted, never parsed (CH16).
+
+**Felt.** "The Grey Company has taken Merewick's coin and marches for Kell." · "The Grey Company sold Merewick out at the ford; Kell's banners rode through." · "Half the Grey Company slipped away in the night." SCRUTINY: its band, terms, three reasons.
+
+**Tier.** `paragonCorpsEnabled` over `paragonsEnabled` + WC's `freeCompaniesEnabled` (WC-10..WC-12, unbuilt — WC's status of record lists only WC-0A..WC-0E built dark) + `warLayerEnabled`; until WC-10 lands, a corps cannot be introduced (the DM's door offers `person` only). DEGRADED ARM: none — no corps. FIRST-VISIBLE: the corps' first retainer card. This closes WC §1.12.5 (e)'s parked force market into CH (the owner's word); the fold's WC inbox carries the row.
